# PreTeXt Authoring Rules

Rules for writing and maintaining PreTeXt XML documents.

## 1. Document Structure

- Root element: `<pretext>` with XML namespace declaration.
- Include `<frontmatter>`, `<chapter>`, `<appendix>`, `<backmatter>` as top-level divisions.
- Use `<xi:include href="chapters/file.ptx"/>` for modular chapter files.
- Define `xml:id` on all major elements (chapters, sections, figures, tables, equations) for cross-referencing.

## 2. Content Elements

- `<p>`: Paragraph text. Do not nest block elements inside `<p>`.
- `<title>`: Always the first child of sectioning elements.
- `<em>` / `<bold>`: Inline emphasis. Do not use for structural headings.
- `<list type="bulleted|numbered|description">`: Lists with `<li>` items.
- `<figure>`: Contains `<image>` and optional `<caption>` and `<description>`.
- `<table>`: Use `<tabular>` for data tables with `<row>` and `<cell>`.
- `<equation>` / `<math>`: Mathematical expressions in LaTeX notation.
- `<code>`: Inline code. `<pre>`: Code blocks.

## 3. Cross-References and Citations

- `<xref ref="ch:overview"/>`: Cross-reference to any element with `xml:id`.
- `<cite ref="bib:key"/>`: Bibliography citation referencing `<biblio>` entries.
- `<url href="..."/>`: External hyperlinks.
- Always verify references by rebuilding: `pretext build`.
- Warnings on broken references are build errors, not suggestions — fix them.

## 4. Build and Validation

- `pretext build html`: Generate HTML output for review.
- `pretext build pdf`: Generate PDF via LaTeX (requires TeX Live).
- `pretext build latex`: Generate LaTeX intermediary (useful for debugging).
- Run `pretext build` before each commit to validate XML and references.
- Never commit a .ptx file that doesn't pass `pretext build`.

## 5. Publisher Configuration

- Place publisher configuration in `publication.ptx` at project root.
- Configure output-specific settings (CSS for HTML, LaTeX preamble for PDF, styles for DOCX).
- Set `@xml:lang` appropriately for language-specific hyphenation and typography.
- Chinese documents: ensure CJK font configuration in the LaTeX preamble for PDF output.

## 6. Accessibility

- Every `<figure>` must have a `<description>` for screen readers.
- Every `<table>` must have `<title>` and column headers.
- Use semantic markup (`<em>`, `<strong>`, `<cite>`) rather than visual formatting.
- Ensure color is not the sole means of conveying information in diagrams.
